<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-export SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/evernote-export4.dtd">
<en-export export-date="20260101T000000Z" application="Evernote" version="10.91.1">
<note><title>Code blocks with a language</title><content><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Evernote names the language the way Prism does.</div><div style="--en-codeblock:true;--en-codeblockLanguage:clike;box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; font-family: Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, &quot;Courier New&quot;, monospace; background-color: rgb(251, 250, 248);">int a = 0x123;  int b = a&lt;&lt;2;</div><div>A block the user left unhighlighted.</div><div style="--en-codeblock:true;--en-codeblockLanguage:plaintext;box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; font-family: Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, &quot;Courier New&quot;, monospace;">just some text</div><div>A block from before Evernote could highlight one.</div><div style="-en-codeblock:true;box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px; font-family: Monaco, Menlo, Consolas, &quot;Courier New&quot;, monospace;"><div>print('Hello, world!')</div></div><div>A language no fence can carry.</div><div style="--en-codeblock:true;--en-codeblockLanguage:objective c;box-sizing: border-box; padding: 8px;">NSLog(@"hi");</div></en-note>]]></content><created>20250310T101500Z</created><updated>20250311T081200Z</updated></note>
</en-export>
